## Unmodified SDKs through the gateway

Does a stock client stream a reply through the gateway, whichever wire
format it speaks and whichever backend serves it? Command: `make sdk-smoke`
(`eval/sdk/smoke.sh`), raw files in `eval/results/sdk-smoke/`. Each case
streams one short prompt and then makes the same request without streaming;
it passes when the SDK's own parser delivered the text in more than one
chunk with a stop reason and usage, and the non-streamed call returned text.
`-via-messages` is the same Ollama model reached through the gateway's
Anthropic provider and Ollama's `/v1/messages`, so the four rows per model
cover every client × backend translation. TTFT is one sample, measured in
the client, and says nothing about the gateway's overhead (Q1 does).

Not measured yet. Start Ollama with `qwen2.5:0.5b`, run `make sdk-smoke`, then `make results`.

## Known problems

Measured weaknesses and cases the runs could not reach, each with what was
observed.

- Budget reconciliation under a flapping store: not measured yet
  (`make chaos-flap`).
- **About two seconds degraded after Redis comes back.** go-redis's
  dial backoff and the gateway's one-second probe run one after the
  other, so a replica keeps using its local limits, grace and no cache for
  about two seconds after Redis is ready (M9, every mode). The cache is
  the visible cost: hits lost, not wrong answers.
- **`everysec` can lose the last second of charges to a machine crash.**
  A killed Redis process loses nothing it acknowledged (the kernel holds
  the written bytes), which is the case M9's container kill tested; a
  crash of the machine or kernel in the middle of a key's spending
  forgets up to about a second of its writes, and no run here produces
  one. With no append-only file (`REDIS_PERSIST=none`, Q6) a restart
  forgets every budget.
- **A `LOADING` Redis was not reached under load.** M9's append-only file
  loaded in tens of milliseconds and no replica called during it; the integration
  test shows a `LOADING` reply degrades like an unreachable store and
  recovers, but no chaos run has a Redis that loads for seconds.

